      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-23_WidnesExaminer_art0107" n="art0107">
        <head>RUNCORN MAN'S RAILWAY FRAUD.</head>
        <p>RUNCORN MAN'S RAILWAY FRAUD.</p>
        <p>Robert Bond, a labourer, 10, John-stre3t, Runcorn, was charged at Wrexham, on Tuesday, with travelling on the Great-Western Railway without previously pay- ing his fare and with intent to avoid payment thereof, and also with giving a false name and address.—The defendant, who pleaded guilty, travelled by the mid- night train from Chester to Wrexham on the Bth ult., and when asked for his ticket at the latter station he said he had only been on the platform to meet a friend. The collector obtained from him what purported to be his name and address, but these were subsequently found to be false.—He was ordered to pay 295., includ- ing costs.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-23_WidnesExaminer_art0108" n="art0108">
