        <p>"I have had a terrible attack of in- fluenia, and my throat and nose had given me shocking pain. One night I awoke with my tongue and throat so swollen and burning that I was unable to breathe or swallow. I applied with an ivory paper knife a piece of Cuticura Ointment to my tongue, and to my sur- prise it melted and percolated down my throat without any effort to swallow, and immediately there was relief. The Cutiaiura Ointment lessened the swelling and fasiLd a passage. I melted pieces of Cuticula Ointment in warm wal and injected it through the nest! This not only gave relief but stopp.;..l the dreadful headache. In two days all pain was gone and also my chest relieved. Cuticura Ointment leaves no bad taste and dissolves and penetrates without any effort to swallow, and it moistens and cools the throat.</p>
        <p>"I think it is wonderful, for relief is almost immediate. I have used Cuticurs, for years for myself and children, but I did not think it could be used internally. My worst trouble was my throat. Largo scarlet pimples like small peas covered the back of my tongue and down my throat, making breathing painful and swallowing difficult, but the Cuticura Ointment worked like magic. I would have been dangerously ill had it not been for Cuticura. It also saved me, probably, a doctor's bill of about £2O. Use my letter if you wish, I only want this fact known to every one. Mrs. Eugenie de Parravicini, 13 Alexander Road, Wim- bledon, April 19 and 25, 1906."</p>
        <p>NOTE.—Thle letter is published to show the value of Cutteura Ointment in the treatment of the mucous membrane.</p>
