      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-23_WidnesExaminer_art0142" n="art0142">
        <head>AT THE TOWN PALL.</head>
        <p>AT THE TOWN PALL.</p>
        <p>THE LUNCHEON.</p>
        <p>Sir Redvers Buller on the Encouragement of Volunteers.</p>
        <p>SOUTH LANCASHIRES COMPLIMENTED.</p>
        <p>j The luncheon in the Parr Hall was a very successful function, and was the occasion of some interesting speeches. The catering was in the able hands of Mr. Powis. The public were admitted to the galleries on payment of a small charge, and a large number availed themselves of the opportunity of attending. The band of the 2nd South Lancashire Regiment was in attend- ! ance and played a choice selection of music. Mr. Henry 1 Roberts presided, and on his right was General Buller and on the left Mrs.Legh and the Mayor and Mayoress. ! There were also present Lieutenant-Colonel Legh, I Viscountess Ikerrin, Colonel and Mrs. Verschoyle, Lieutenant-Colonel Hall, Colonel Adam, Colonel Richardson, Brigadier-General Fry, Mrs. Henry Roberts, Mr. and Mrs. Drury, Colonel and Mrs. Edelsten, Colonel Ridgway, the Town Clerk (Mr. J. Lyon-Whittle), Colonel Cook, Colonel Buckton, Mrs. Buckton, Major B. Fairclough, Major Bundock, Major Appleton, Major Widdowes and Mrs. Widdowes, Major and Mrs. Steavenson, Major Roome, Captain Pilkington, Captain Carey, Captain Solly Flood, Captain G. R. Crosfield, Captain Carlyon, Captain Owen, Cap- tain Dawson, Captain Colville, Captain Wilkin- son, Captain Roberts, Captain Potter and Mrs. ! Potter, Captain Eckersley, Captain Osborne, Cap- ! tam n and Mrs. Oakley, Captain and Quarter-Master I Whitfield, Captain Ritchie, Captain Goren, Captain , Clarke-Jervoise, Lieutenants Wynn, Drew, Haseldine, Callard, Koster, Wesche, Hutchinson, O'Leary, Morgan, Bayley, Shaw, Stannard, Stewart, R. Roberts, Quarter- ! Master and Mrs. Bailey, Quarter-Master and Mrs. Roberts, Mr. A. H. Crosfield, M.P., Mr. R. Pierpoint, ! Mrs. Pierpoint, the Rector (the Rev. Canon Willis),Mrs. j Willis, Rev. H. V. and Mrs. Pio•bot, Rev. W. and Mrs' I Bracecamp, Rev. Father Wilson,Rev.D.Considine. Alder- man and Mrs.Forshaw,Councillors Dr. Joseph, Fulton Smith,Ellison,Wilkinson, Dr. Mrs. and Miss Adams, Mr. and Mrs. W.Peter Rylands, Mrs. Crosfleld, Mr. and Mrs. IHenry Greenall