      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-23_WidnesExaminer_art0145" n="art0145">
        <head>Statue.</head>
        <p>The Statue.</p>
        <p>The statue, which is the work of Mr. Alfred Drury, A.R.A., is a very striking specimen of the sculptor's art. It gives a life-like representation of Colonel MacCarthy O'Leary, the late gallant commander of the South Lancashire Regiment, who fell whilst leading his men at Pieter's Hill. He is depicted in the attitude in which he appeared at the fateful charge, having in one band his field-glasses while with the other he grasps a carbine. The pedestal is oE granite and bears bronze panels containing a suitable incription, a list of the South Lancashire soldiers who lost their lives in the South African campaign, and a record of the engage- ments in which the regiment took Rut. Surmounting the list of the fallen is a representation of the angel of death hovering over a woman and child. The following are the names placed on record :</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-02-23_WidnesExaminer_art0146" n="art0146">
        <head>SOUTH LANCASHIRE REGIMENT.</head>
        <p>SOUTH LANCASHIRE REGIMENT.</p>
        <p>Officers,Non-Commissioned Officers and men who gave their lives for their country during the war in South Africa 1899-1902.</p>
        <p>LINE BATTALION. OFFICERS.</p>
        <p>Lieutenant-Colonel W. MacCarthy O'Leary (who felt leading the charge on Pieter's Hill, 27th February, 1900.) Lieut. F. itt. Raphael H R Kane ,FFICERS AND MEN. „ W. Doyle „ G. Duckworth „ J. Duffey „ J. Dutubill „ J. Fagan „ T. Farmer „ NV. R. Farquhar „ IV. Ferber „ W. A. Ford „ A. Garlish „ R. Garnett „ W. Gellor „ R. Goulding „ P. Graney „ C. Gredant „ J. Hall „ C. Harding „ L. H. Haywood J. Heaton G. Heron W. Higgins P. Hogan R. E. Howich J. Hughes E. Ingman D. Irwin J. Jackson I. Jeffries T. W. Jennings E. Johnson j. Johnson E. Joncs M. Jones 11. Jones S. Jones T. Jones NV: Jones P. Keane R. Keati, g T. Lambe.t J. Leslie J. Lynch P. Maloney W. Mcßride J. McDonald J. Neilson E. O'Neil I'. Parker E. Pennington R. Penningtnn</p>
        <p>Captain N. M. Lynch „ C. G. F. G. Birch NON COMMISSIONED Q-M. Sergt. C.H.Barrow Sergt. G. Penwill „ J. Candy „ S. Bridge „ G. Gray „ H. Heppenstall „ T. Orr „ A. Thomas „ W. El. Wheatley „ J. Whittaker „ J. Threlfall Lance-Sergt. A. I'. Thorpe • T. Kirsrade • J. Hesketh H. Monks » Corpl. D. Connolly „ W. Neilson „ T. Worrall „ A. Williams „ J. Lapping „ E. Rae Lance-Corp. J. Barnfather lf f t J. Darn •f fl T. Smith P H Chapman ft » Dr. F. J. Hackett „ G. T. McGaragle Private J. Aldred • „ J. Armitage „ J. Astbury „ A. Beer „ H. Birkenhead )9 H. Birkett „ G. M. Braid „ J. Beanwell „ E. Brennan „ R. Brown „ T. Brown „ A. Canning „ J. Canning „ A. Cantrell</p>
