        <p>PADCATE. WESLEY. GUILD.—The Rev. W. Mellor presided over the Guild meeting on Monday evening, when a descrip- tive lecture, illustrated by lime-light views, was given by Miss Emily Bennett, of Grange Mount, entitled " Memories of Venice. Verona and the Italian lakes." As Miss Bennett has recently returned from a tour in Italy she was able to give n graphic description of Venice with its canals and its quaint and narrow streets, its grim old feudal tower's and stately palaces, speaking eloquently of the past when the Scaligers reigned supreme. Miss Bennett also related some episodes,both startling and amusing, of her journey.</p>
